<$fill $name="body">

!! What it does

A dock in a corner of the page shows how many things need you. Each count is an //area//: a config tiddler with a filter, for example "tasks overdue", "due today", "started". Click the dock and a panel lists the items. Press an item and drag it sideways: a half ring of action tiles opens. Hover a group (Move, Mute, Status, …) to fan out its tiles, release on one to run it. The item is not opened.

The plugin knows nothing about your data. Areas, extra actions and extra groups are config tiddlers in your wiki.

!! How you use it

# The dock shows one pill per area that has items (alert, then warning, then hint) and the time of the last check. ↻ checks again.
# Click the dock: the panel opens. Tabs appear when areas name different tabs. An area shows 5 items, then "+ N more".
# Click an item to open it. The panel stays open, so you can triage.
# Press an item, drag more than 5 pixels (touch: hold 400 ms, then drag). The ring opens on the side of the panel that faces free space.
# Hover a group for 150 ms: its tiles fan out. Release on a tile to run it, or on a group to run its default tile. Esc, release elsewhere, or losing the window cancels.
# The item stays in the panel with a mark ("→ Mon 9", "🔕 until Mon 9") until the next check.
# Click outside the panel to close it. Esc closes it too.

!! Counts are a snapshot

The area filters run on reload, on ↻ and after an action. They never run while you edit, so the dock costs nothing while you type. Edit a date and the counts stay until you check again.

!! Where the configuration lives

|!What |!Where |
|Areas |tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/area` |
|Groups of the ring |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/group` |
|Actions (tiles) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/action` |
|Recipes (action templates) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/recipe` |
|Info parts (lines under an item) |tag `$:/tags/rimir/work-focus/info-part` |
|Settings |`$:/config/rimir/work-focus/*` (see the settings tab) |

See //Reference// for every field and //Examples// for ready configurations.

</$fill>
